 "how_to_row_against_it": {
  "scope": "Every row names its format. A core runs the rows whose format is in its own set (core_formats, from MIG-7) and records the rest n/a (format); for file rows it expects a refusal instead, see refusals. A calls row runs where its entry_point is one of the core's own (core_entry_points) and is recorded n/a (entry point) elsewhere: entry points belong to a core, not to a format, so a core that reads gettext files need not have Django's gettext() call. Expected values in rows outside the JS set are derived from MIG-2 and MIG-4 and confirmed by the lane that runs them; a lane that disagrees records it and the owner reconciles, never the vendored copy.",
  "value_conversion": "convert(value, format) must yield expected, with recognised as given. When recognised is false the phrase is the value exactly as written, and the SDK warns.",
  "plural_forms": "Forms keyed by category — i18next's suffix pairs, a rails-i18n count hash (zero, 0, 1, one, ..., other), a gettext msgid/msgid_plural pair — convert to expected. Exact branches first ascending, then zero, one, two, few, many, other; the number is # inside branches.",
  "calls": "A literal miss (MIG-2) through entry_point converts to expected. same_phrase_as names a row that must register the identical phrase. category, when present, is the category the call registers under.",
  "resolution": "Resolving key against files (in order) yields expected: the phrase, the category (category_arg, when given, is passed by the call and wins), the answering file and recognised; null is the miss. A file with no format is plain.",
  "refusals": "A core whose set does not include format refuses the file at load with an error naming the format and the file. A .mo file is refused by every core, naming its .po."
 },
